WEBVTT

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:15.290
Recording

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:23.040
Recording

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:25.040
Kasumi
Got an idea for our new song.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:27.420
Fun and sparkly /
We're all connected /
Our music is our bond /
We've been through tough times /
But today is the greatest!
Let our sounds ring together /
So they reach everyone /
Even if we lose sight of each other or drift apart /
We can find each other again...
Something like that?

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:30.750
"Find each other again"...

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:51.580
I think you'll understand once you listen to my band.

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:33.420
Culture Festival and Show To-Do List
1. Choose date for self-sponsored show --> Saturday, end of June
2. Turn in culture festival show application to student council (done!)
3. Reserve live venue, Galaxy! OK to start night before.
4. Choose name for self-sponsored show 
5. Negotiate with guest bands

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:33.420
6. Create time schedule
7. Decide on set list for culture festival and self-sponsored show!
*See if we can hand out and post up around the venue!
8. Create tickets (pre-orders, reservations, etc.)
9. Costumes! (maybe ask Rinko-senpai for advice)
Don't forget the set-up list!

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:38.460
Arisa made this to-do list for us, but we'll need to
divide up the work to get all of it done.

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:40.920
Which one of these needs to be done ASAP?

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:42.290
Probably the fliers.

00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:45.750
If we wait too long to announce it,
no one will be able to come.

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:48.000
Okay, let's start making those then.

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:54.040
Sorry I'm late!

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:56.130
No prob! Wanna play?

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:58.040
You go ahead and get set up.

00:02:58.040 --> 00:02:59.580
'Kay. O-Tae!

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:02.580
Everything okay?

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:06.790
I want to play with another band.

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:07.710
What?

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:13.790
What do you mean?

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:18.210
I want to... practice more.

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:23.960
I really want to polish my skills
for our self-sponsored show.

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:26.630
What sort of band?

00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:29.880
My friend Lay's band.

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:31.830
We grew up together.

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:33.440
Your old friend?

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:36.270
They really need a guitarist.

00:03:36.580 --> 00:03:39.710
Oh, okay. So you'd be a support guitarist.

00:03:39.710 --> 00:03:40.750
Support?

00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:46.080
Yeah. Talented people who get called in
to join temporarily to fill in missing roles.

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:47.990
O-Tae, that's amazing!

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:50.540
Jeez, don't scare me like that!

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:52.370
I thought you were quitting PoPiPa.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:57.000
They gave me a demo to listen to.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:59.880
It was... intense.

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:01.300
Like getting shocked.

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:04.040
I want to be able to sound like that too.

00:04:08.170 --> 00:04:09.330
All right!

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:12.380
I'm gonna do my best to practice and prepare here.

00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:14.290
You give guitar training your all too, O-Tae!

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:18.190
I'll do my best.

00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:17.420
I'm here.

00:05:27.170 --> 00:05:28.250
Whoa...

00:05:28.250 --> 00:05:29.670
Welcome.

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:34.850
Are you the friend Layer-san told us about?

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:35.960
I'm Tae Ha-

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:38.290
You must be Tae Hanazono.

00:05:42.670 --> 00:05:45.000
I'm the producer, CHU2.

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:48.280
This is Pareo, and that's Masking over there.

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:52.580
Is Lay-

00:05:52.580 --> 00:05:54.420
Layer is at work.

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:57.460
She's still under an old contract,
so there's nothing we can do.

00:05:57.460 --> 00:05:59.580
But after tomorrow, it'll be no problem!

00:06:03.460 --> 00:06:04.960
Tae Hanazono?

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:06.790
That's her. How 'bout the demo?

00:06:06.790 --> 00:06:07.960
I gave it a listen.

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:09.540
Well, can you do-

00:06:09.540 --> 00:06:10.470
Ouch!

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:11.670
Pareo!

00:06:11.670 --> 00:06:13.170
Coming, Mistress!

00:06:14.210 --> 00:06:16.210
I won't take just anybody.

00:06:16.210 --> 00:06:19.540
If you can't play the music
I want to hear, you can leave.

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:20.650
Ready?

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:23.080
N-not lady...

00:06:23.080 --> 00:06:24.820
I am a girl.

00:06:26.130 --> 00:06:27.710
...Okay, then.

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:30.420
Arisa, wait for me!

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:30.420
Double
Culture
Festival

00:06:30.420 --> 00:06:34.880
Hurry up! If we miss the train, we'll have to sprint
for two stations all the way to Haneoka!

00:06:36.290 --> 00:06:40.540
It's so tiring running back and forth
between Hanasakigawa and Haneoka!

00:06:47.880 --> 00:06:52.670
All done! If I can finish one more,
maybe I can go to the warehouse today!

00:06:52.670 --> 00:06:54.920
Can somebody grab the tape for me?

00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:55.970
Oh, sure.

00:06:58.250 --> 00:07:00.580
Can you come over here for a minute next?

00:07:00.580 --> 00:07:01.290
What?
Sorry! We need you to make two more ghosts!

00:07:01.290 --> 00:07:03.210
Sorry! We need you to make two more ghosts!

00:07:03.210 --> 00:07:03.920
Wha...

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:05.380
Oh no...

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:07.250
I'm gonna take out the trash, okay?

00:07:07.250 --> 00:07:08.750
Need some help, Saaya?

00:07:08.750 --> 00:07:10.570
You're the best, Natsuki.

00:07:11.960 --> 00:07:13.960
Rimi-chan looked pretty panicked.

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:18.130
We've been pretty busy preparing for
the culture festival and our live shows.

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:23.080
At this rate, we're gonna fall
out of step with each other...

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:24.290
It's scary.

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:33.290
Is everything all right with Poppin' Party?

00:07:33.290 --> 00:07:35.630
Yeah. I talked to them about it.

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:38.600
So you're gonna join the band, then?

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:40.130
Mhmm.

00:07:40.130 --> 00:07:44.960
I don't think I've been that nervous for a test
since entrance exams or auditioning at Space.

00:07:47.210 --> 00:07:51.290
I wasn't sure if I'd be able to play
as good as that demo.

00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:53.920
I heard you played pretty solid.

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:57.380
I knew that if I failed, I couldn't join you, Lay- Layer.

00:07:57.380 --> 00:07:58.790
Lay is fine.

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:02.750
I've been waiting a long time.
For us to play together again.

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:05.960
I want to hear you play.

00:08:12.670 --> 00:08:14.170
Any requests?

00:08:14.540 --> 00:08:15.750
THAT song.

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:27.750
Adding a map to Galaxy seems like
the nice thing to do.

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:30.960
From the station, walk straight about 200 steps!

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:30.960
Station Galaxy!!
Market Street

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:36.250
I'm back.

00:08:36.250 --> 00:08:37.630
Welcome!

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:39.710
Where is everyone?

00:08:39.710 --> 00:08:42.250
They're all still busy prepping...

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:43.540
Want a snack?

00:08:43.540 --> 00:08:44.540
Sure.

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:46.630
How was playing support guitar?

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:48.250
Mm...

00:08:48.790 --> 00:08:50.210
You look tired.

00:08:52.750 --> 00:08:53.840
How about you?

00:08:53.840 --> 00:08:55.250
Overloaded...

00:08:55.250 --> 00:08:57.290
I've gotta go to Haneoka again tomorrow.

00:08:57.290 --> 00:08:58.880
To help Arisa?

00:08:58.880 --> 00:09:00.000
Yeah.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.600
Saaya and Rimi-rin are super busy too,

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:04.930
but they said they've been doing lots of solo practice!

00:09:04.930 --> 00:09:06.920
Oh! That reminds me!

00:09:09.460 --> 00:09:11.920
Look, I picked out the song I want us to play live!

00:09:11.920 --> 00:09:13.000
For which show?

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:14.040
Both!

00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:15.630
Self-Sponsored Show Set List
1. Happy Happy Party!
2. Kirakira da to ka Yume da to ka ~Sing Girls~
3. New song!
4. Teardrops

00:09:14.040 --> 00:09:15.630
Culture Festival Set List
1. Kirakira da to ka Yume da to ka ~Sing Girls~
2. Mae e Susume!
3. Happy Happy Party!
4. STAR=BEAT! ~Hoshi no Kodou~

00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:20.540
But, I don't have a riff for the new song yet...

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:23.380
It's okay! We've still got time.

00:09:25.420 --> 00:09:27.580
All of you are trying so hard...

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:36.000
Maybe I can try to work on the song too!

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:38.130
I've only ever relied on you for that stuff.

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:39.920
I can do lyrics too!

00:09:41.920 --> 00:09:43.540
Ooh, a star!

00:09:43.540 --> 00:09:44.790
Do you want it, O-Tae?

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:50.790
Good night.

00:09:52.130 --> 00:09:56.540
You're Not Alone

00:10:00.420 --> 00:10:02.420
Recording

00:10:06.420 --> 00:10:08.420
My name is O-Tae...

00:10:15.880 --> 00:10:17.540
What are you doing?!

00:10:17.540 --> 00:10:21.540
O-Tae does this thing with her guitar
when she's writing music, huh.

00:10:21.540 --> 00:10:22.460
So?

00:10:22.460 --> 00:10:23.460
I tried doing it.

00:10:23.460 --> 00:10:24.220
And?

00:10:24.880 --> 00:10:26.290
It was terrible.

00:10:26.290 --> 00:10:28.710
I'm sure. Why don't you talk to Rimi?

00:10:28.710 --> 00:10:31.210
She looked really busy...

00:10:31.210 --> 00:10:32.250
Hm.

00:10:32.540 --> 00:10:35.250
Okay, I get that you want to help out O-Tae.

00:10:35.250 --> 00:10:37.750
And now, you can take these!

00:10:38.750 --> 00:10:40.000
Fine...

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:44.000
Haneoka Girls' Academy
Hanasakigawa Girls' Academy
Double Culture Festival

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:46.450
Okay, let's write a new song.

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:55.750
But we don't have anyone here that can write.

00:10:55.750 --> 00:10:57.260
We'll work it out somehow.

00:10:57.630 --> 00:10:59.630
How does Afterglow write songs?

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:00.790
Huh?

00:11:00.790 --> 00:11:03.670
Ran does it, just like always...

00:11:04.920 --> 00:11:09.750
And it always makes her even grouchier than normal.

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:12.210
How about Hello-Happy?

00:11:12.210 --> 00:11:14.730
With us, it's Misaki-chan...

00:11:15.960 --> 00:11:18.460
She knows how to connect our ideas.

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:20.380
What about Roselia?

00:11:20.380 --> 00:11:25.130
Well, Yukina keeps the light in her room on all night...

00:11:26.670 --> 00:11:29.750
Maybe she's... praying?

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:31.750
Interesting...

00:11:32.170 --> 00:11:33.420
Kasumi-chan?!

00:11:33.420 --> 00:11:36.590
Uhh, I wanted to learn about songwriting...

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:38.080
Oh, really?

00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:42.180
In any case, why don't we start by figuring out
what kind of song we want it to be?

00:11:42.180 --> 00:11:44.140
A theme, huh...

00:11:44.460 --> 00:11:46.220
Hina-chan, do you have any advice?

00:11:46.220 --> 00:11:47.630
How about part-timing?

00:11:47.630 --> 00:11:49.500
Oh! Good one!

00:11:49.500 --> 00:11:51.960
I help out my family at home too.

00:11:51.960 --> 00:11:54.500
Everyone here works part-time, huh...

00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:57.080
How about something to
cheer people up at work, then?

00:11:57.080 --> 00:11:58.580
That could be good!

00:11:59.920 --> 00:12:01.210
Tee-hee!

00:12:02.580 --> 00:12:03.710
I'm back.

00:12:03.710 --> 00:12:07.330
Well, you took so long your tea's all cold now.

00:12:08.170 --> 00:12:09.160
Huh?

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:14.420
What are you doing...?

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:17.460
I'm songwriting.

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:19.710
Oh jeez...

00:12:23.630 --> 00:12:25.830
I guess I'll make more tea.

00:12:34.100 --> 00:12:36.420
There you are, Rinrin!

00:12:37.080 --> 00:12:38.380
Ako-chan.

00:12:38.830 --> 00:12:42.080
Feels kinda weird seeing you here at Haneoka, Rinrin.

00:12:42.080 --> 00:12:43.080
Yeah.

00:12:44.170 --> 00:12:45.830
Are you okay?

00:12:46.670 --> 00:12:47.920
I'm fine.

00:12:47.920 --> 00:12:52.000
I have to talk to a lot of different people,
so that's been tough...

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:53.830
but they've all been approaching me...

00:12:53.830 --> 00:12:55.380
Sorry, Prez!

00:12:55.380 --> 00:12:57.960
Where are we supposed to take these boxes again?

00:12:57.960 --> 00:12:59.750
The storage under the stage.

00:12:59.750 --> 00:13:00.710
All of them?

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:02.710
Y-yes. If you could, please.

00:13:02.710 --> 00:13:05.670
Okay. She said we need all of these!

00:13:05.670 --> 00:13:07.500
You look like a real student council prez!

00:13:07.500 --> 00:13:09.040
Y-you think so?

00:13:09.540 --> 00:13:12.210
I... I've been worried...

00:13:12.210 --> 00:13:15.670
about whether or not I can do a good job
with the double culture festival.

00:13:15.670 --> 00:13:17.580
Well, you just gave good instructions.

00:13:17.580 --> 00:13:22.130
Y-yeah. I just hope I can keep this up
until we're all done...

00:13:22.130 --> 00:13:23.580
You'll do great!

00:13:23.580 --> 00:13:25.110
It's not exactly our game,

00:13:25.110 --> 00:13:28.120
but you can think of this
like gaining experience points to level up!

00:13:28.130 --> 00:13:33.580
Aw... I haven't been able to play
the special event content at all...

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:37.330
Let me worry about that, okay?
You keep doing your best here!

00:13:37.330 --> 00:13:40.460
I'll still be your party member
no matter what happens!

00:13:42.170 --> 00:13:43.040
Okay.

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:46.750
Open to everyone!
Solo players and beginners welcome!

00:13:46.750 --> 00:13:47.960
Cat Café
Meow

00:13:47.960 --> 00:13:49.330
Go-Cart Course
This Way!!

00:13:49.330 --> 00:13:50.930
A fleeting moment just for you
Kaoru Cafe

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:54.930
Want to join a band?

00:13:57.040 --> 00:13:59.250
Not a single person...

00:13:59.670 --> 00:14:03.580
It's a miracle I got to play in a band
in middle school at all.

00:14:03.580 --> 00:14:05.000
Hey, Rokka.

00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:05.820
Huh?

00:14:07.250 --> 00:14:08.830
Lisa-senpai!

00:14:08.830 --> 00:14:11.130
Still looking for members, huh?

00:14:11.420 --> 00:14:13.540
I really want to perform at the festival...

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:14.880
I see.

00:14:16.250 --> 00:14:17.210
Here!

00:14:17.210 --> 00:14:20.250
Th-thank you!

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:22.840
Where's my wallet...

00:14:22.840 --> 00:14:24.920
Don't worry about it. My treat!

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:28.330
Th-thank you. Th-that's nice of you.

00:14:30.920 --> 00:14:34.290
Are you here to practice for
your culture festival band?

00:14:34.290 --> 00:14:38.040
Yep. It feels kind of refreshing
to play with some new faces.

00:14:38.540 --> 00:14:40.830
It's fun getting to see what everyone else can do...

00:14:40.830 --> 00:14:43.410
discovering what makes us all different.

00:14:43.790 --> 00:14:45.110
Drink, drink!

00:14:49.040 --> 00:14:50.880
Whoa, that's sweet.

00:14:50.880 --> 00:14:52.500
Yep, that was for Yukina.

00:14:52.960 --> 00:14:55.040
A-and you gave it to m-me?

00:14:55.500 --> 00:14:58.670
To be honest, I wanted to play
with Roselia at the festival,

00:14:58.670 --> 00:15:01.040
but Yukina's not really into this sort of thing.

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:02.380
Too fun for her.

00:15:03.540 --> 00:15:06.420
Then why is Yukina-senpai...

00:15:06.420 --> 00:15:07.380
Hm?

00:15:07.790 --> 00:15:12.000
Um, what made you and the others
decide to form a band originally?

00:15:12.500 --> 00:15:14.220
I, um...

00:15:14.920 --> 00:15:19.250
I always thought that people
played in bands because it's fun...

00:15:26.130 --> 00:15:28.250
Kasumi, watch your step.

00:15:28.250 --> 00:15:29.280
I will!

00:15:29.280 --> 00:15:31.500
Rimi-rin, want me to take one of those?

00:15:31.500 --> 00:15:32.960
I'm fine.

00:15:39.210 --> 00:15:40.830
Yukina-senpai!

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:42.330
Go on ahead of me!

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:42.960
'Kay.

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:43.920
Kasumi?

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:47.040
Yukina-senpai!

00:15:48.630 --> 00:15:50.040
Is that for the culture festival?

00:15:50.040 --> 00:15:52.840
Yep! We're performing live there too.

00:15:53.250 --> 00:15:54.800
What about your self-sponsored one?

00:15:55.540 --> 00:15:57.330
We're still doing that show too.

00:15:57.330 --> 00:16:00.100
We're planning it together, step by step.

00:16:01.170 --> 00:16:02.170
I see.

00:16:02.540 --> 00:16:06.330
We play in Roselia... because we've all got a dream.

00:16:06.330 --> 00:16:07.460
A dream?

00:16:09.380 --> 00:16:11.380
The Future World Fest.

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:14.210
It's a really huge music festival...

00:16:14.210 --> 00:16:17.210
our biggest dream is to perform
as one of the top acts.

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:21.160
It's the reason we self-sponsor shows
and do guest performances.

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:25.420
It started off as only Yukina's dream,

00:16:25.420 --> 00:16:28.290
but now it's a dream all five of us share.

00:16:31.540 --> 00:16:33.630
Aw, now I'm just rambling...

00:16:33.630 --> 00:16:35.290
Not at all! That's beautiful!

00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:37.170
Thanks.

00:16:37.510 --> 00:16:39.140
Yukina-senpai.

00:16:39.330 --> 00:16:43.540
If it's okay with you, we'd love to ask
Roselia to perform with us.

00:16:43.540 --> 00:16:45.600
At our self-sponsored show.

00:16:47.920 --> 00:16:49.330
I'll think about it.

00:16:50.920 --> 00:16:52.500
Thank you!

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:04.870
Haneoka Girls' Academy
Hanasakigawa Girls' Academy
Double Culture Festival

00:17:06.830 --> 00:17:08.170
There she is.

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:09.550
Kasumi-chan!

00:17:09.550 --> 00:17:10.670
I'm sorry!

00:17:10.670 --> 00:17:12.290
What were you two talking about?

00:17:14.880 --> 00:17:15.680
Huh?

00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:22.460
Everyone, we're going to have an open rehearsal
for the festival session band!

00:17:22.460 --> 00:17:25.040
Please, join us in the auditorium!

00:17:25.040 --> 00:17:29.040
No pushing, no running, and don't follow strangers!

00:17:29.380 --> 00:17:30.790
That trickster...

00:17:30.790 --> 00:17:35.210
Hina told us there'd be a rehearsal,
but not that it would be open to the public!

00:17:40.330 --> 00:17:41.460
Whoa!

00:17:41.460 --> 00:17:42.630
Look at that!

00:17:42.630 --> 00:17:44.080
It's like a pre-event!

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:45.830
We've still got days to go...

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:48.130
A Pre-pre-pre-pre-pre-pre-pre-event then!

00:17:48.130 --> 00:17:49.540
That's a mouthful.

00:17:53.500 --> 00:17:58.080
Since it's our last high school festival,
we wanted to make it the greatest one ever!

00:17:58.080 --> 00:17:59.830
S-so we created a special...

00:17:59.830 --> 00:18:00.830
You've got this!

00:18:00.830 --> 00:18:01.880
...a spechal band!

00:18:01.880 --> 00:18:03.060
Whoops!

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:04.680
She's so cute!

00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:06.830
You can do it, Aya-chan!

00:18:06.830 --> 00:18:07.830
No worries!

00:18:07.830 --> 00:18:11.130
The more you stumble, the quicker you slide...

00:18:11.130 --> 00:18:12.790
That's not very reassuring!

00:18:12.790 --> 00:18:14.500
It's fine, it's fine!

00:18:14.500 --> 00:18:15.630
Come on!

00:18:15.960 --> 00:18:19.960
We hope you like our song.
We made it to cheer up part-timers!

00:20:02.250 --> 00:20:05.080
Let's do our best at the culture festival too, guys!

00:20:05.420 --> 00:20:06.250
Yeah!

00:20:20.540 --> 00:20:22.670
Hana-chan, have some water.

00:20:25.000 --> 00:20:26.000
Thanks.

00:20:28.670 --> 00:20:30.950
I guess you're all right.

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:34.080
Wow! Mass-san never compliments anybody!

00:20:36.540 --> 00:20:38.340
But! You're not there yet!

00:20:38.830 --> 00:20:39.960
Pareo.

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:42.790
Attention, please!

00:20:48.290 --> 00:20:50.750
We are RAISE A SUILEN!

00:20:50.750 --> 00:20:52.540
RAS for short!

00:20:53.210 --> 00:20:55.040
"Suilen"? The flower?

00:20:55.040 --> 00:20:58.630
Would it be clearer if we stick
Japanese bamboo curtains in there?

00:20:58.630 --> 00:21:00.380
Oh, "suilen" as in "bamboo screen"?

00:21:00.380 --> 00:21:03.250
Yes! The meaning behind the name...

00:21:03.250 --> 00:21:04.710
Raise up the screen!

00:21:04.710 --> 00:21:05.540
Yes!

00:21:06.330 --> 00:21:07.830
No! Pareo!

00:21:07.830 --> 00:21:09.630
Just a moment, Mistress!

00:21:14.870 --> 00:21:16.580
RAISE A SUILEN!

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:18.630
By flying a banner with this name,

00:21:18.630 --> 00:21:22.250
we're showing the world that we're
determined to bathe in the spotlight!

00:21:22.630 --> 00:21:27.430
With my top-notch music,
we're putting an end the era of the girl band!

00:21:27.430 --> 00:21:29.880
We're gonna start a whole new world!

00:21:30.470 --> 00:21:33.080
Starting tomorrow, we'll be in the studio every day.

00:21:33.080 --> 00:21:37.580
I'll make sure we're polished perfectly
to explode with our first solo concert!

00:21:38.330 --> 00:21:39.330
Perfect...

00:21:39.330 --> 00:21:41.250
Yes! Perfect!

00:21:41.250 --> 00:21:43.880
We're gonna perform tons of show! Starting with...

00:21:51.880 --> 00:21:53.750
That's the day of the culture festival...

00:23:34.330 --> 00:23:39.080
Next episode: School Festival Symphony
